[{:db/id 17592186198309 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-24815c66-50ab-5aab-ac7b-25ddc673e132" "question-73c135de-ad71-58aa-a780-c01d04341240" "question-aea6db90-17cf-56a2-9d48-5e13d8af9223" "question-bb3ce97a-5535-5c1b-80e8-b47b040c493e" "question-6cb148c3-0ff5-5200-b071-d1495f25735d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198207 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $5 \\mid m$ then $25 \\mid m$\n\n- If $25 \\mid m$ then $10 \\mid m$\n\n- If $25 \\mid m$ then $5 \\mid m$" :question/worked-solution "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$ we have transitivity of divisibility:\n\n$a \\mid b \\quad$ and $\\quad b \\mid c$ $\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad$ $a \\mid c$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. As a counterexample, let ${\\color{blue}{m}}={\\color{blue}{5}}.$ Then, $5\\mid {\\color{blue}{5}}$ but $25\\not \\mid {\\color{blue}{5}}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, let ${\\color{blue}{m}}={\\color{blue}{25}}.$ Then, $25\\mid {\\color{blue}{25}}$ but $10\\not \\mid {\\color{blue}{25}}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, note that $5 \\mid 25.$ Therefore, we have\n$5\\mid 25$ and $25\\mid m,$ which implies that $5 \\mid m.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198310 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-42a248b1-4b2a-5a7f-b673-589ac28da9a8" "question-553ed68f-8e74-5dda-a8b3-cdd3e89c31cb" "question-f3b9fb7f-2262-5e34-bb97-3a915acfa755" "question-360410c4-4e76-5ee1-ae9a-a22c317dc4de"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198202 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $3^3 \\: | \\: 3^2b$ then $3^3 \\: | \\: b$\n\n- If $20 \\: | \\: 30b$ then $20 \\: | \\: b$\n\n- If $2^5 \\: | \\: 3^4b$ then $2^5 \\: | \\: b$" :question/worked-solution "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$c \\:|\\: ab \\quad$ and $\\quad \\text{gcd}(a,c)=1$ $\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad$ $\\quad c \\:|\\: b.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. As a counterexample, let ${\\color{blue}{b}}={\\color{blue}{3}}.$ Then, $3^3\\mid 3^2\\cdot {\\color{blue}{3}}$ but $3^3\\not\\mid {\\color{blue}{3}}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, let ${\\color{blue}{b}}={\\color{blue}{2}}.$ Then, $20\\mid 30\\cdot {\\color{blue}{2}}$ but $20\\not\\mid {\\color{blue}{2}}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(2^5, 3^4)=1.$ Therefore, we have $2^5 \\: | \\: 3^4b$ and $\\text{gcd}(2^5, 3^4)=1,$ which implies $2^5\\: | \\: b.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198311 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5ddd359d-678b-53c8-9991-000fcf922944" "question-6d7153a0-178f-57d1-b332-d3ea8e076028" "question-9f50d1b1-0f30-55bf-aeb5-6bf553fa9e40" "question-237e8d15-d348-5681-a8d5-20db7f138f56"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198203 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $3 \\: | \\: a$ and $21 \\: | \\: a$ then $63 \\: | \\: a$\n\n- If $3 \\: | \\: b$ and $22 \\: | \\: b$ then $66 \\: | \\: b$\n\n- If $2^3 \\: | \\: c$ and $3^2 \\: | \\: c$ then $72 \\: | \\: c$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$a \\:|\\: c,$ $\\quad b \\:|\\: c, \\quad$ and $\\quad \\text{gcd}(a,b)=1$ $\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad$ $ab \\:|\\: c.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. As a counterexample, let ${\\color{blue}{a}}={\\color{blue}{21}}.$ Then, $(3\\mid {\\color{blue}{21}})$ and $(21\\mid {\\color{blue}{21}}),$ but $(63\\not\\mid {\\color{blue}{21}}).$\n\n- Statement II is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(3, 22)=1$ and $3\\cdot 22 = 66.$ Therefore, we have $(3 \\: | \\: b), (22 \\: | \\: b),$ and $\\text{gcd}(3, 22)=1,$ which implies $(66\\: | \\: b).$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(2^3, 3^2)=1$ and $2^3\\cdot 3^2 = 72.$ Therefore, we have $(2^3 \\: | \\: c), (3^2 \\: | \\: c),$ and $\\text{gcd}(2^3, 3^2)=1,$ which implies $(72 \\: | \\: c).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-24815c66-50ab-5aab-ac7b-25ddc673e132" :question/id #uuid "24815c66-50ab-5aab-ac7b-25ddc673e132" :question/math-academy-id "q-221381" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $11∣k$ then $33∣k$\n- If $33∣k$ then $11∣k$\n- If $33∣k$ then $3∣k$" :question/worked-solution "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$ we have transitivity of divisibility:\n\n$a∣b\\,$ and $\\,b∣c$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $a∣c$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. As a counterexample, let $k=11.$ Then, $11∣11$ but $33∤11.$\n\n- Statement II is true. First, note that $11∣33.$ Therefore, we have\n$11∣33$ and $33∣k,$ which implies that $11∣k.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, note that $3∣33.$ Therefore, we have\n$3∣33$ and $33∣k,$ which implies that $3∣k.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a4feefa3-f467-563c-b592-67d4467afe30"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a4feefa3-f467-563c-b592-67d4467afe30" :answer-field/id #uuid "a4feefa3-f467-563c-b592-67d4467afe30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-37d1ed1f-2a27-5962-9f76-7e68504f6b25" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f5c3abe4-7795-5469-8fa0-9b120fc335e2" "answer-92f86242-b5e9-5e13-99b0-1f387aeb933c" "answer-d6e70fa3-3d87-548c-a566-669bf0527f26" "answer-37d1ed1f-2a27-5962-9f76-7e68504f6b25" "answer-a873a377-31d6-5d14-bc3d-af2b01b12bb6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5c3abe4-7795-5469-8fa0-9b120fc335e2" :answer/id #uuid "f5c3abe4-7795-5469-8fa0-9b120fc335e2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92f86242-b5e9-5e13-99b0-1f387aeb933c" :answer/id #uuid "92f86242-b5e9-5e13-99b0-1f387aeb933c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6e70fa3-3d87-548c-a566-669bf0527f26" :answer/id #uuid "d6e70fa3-3d87-548c-a566-669bf0527f26" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37d1ed1f-2a27-5962-9f76-7e68504f6b25" :answer/id #uuid "37d1ed1f-2a27-5962-9f76-7e68504f6b25" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a873a377-31d6-5d14-bc3d-af2b01b12bb6" :answer/id #uuid "a873a377-31d6-5d14-bc3d-af2b01b12bb6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-73c135de-ad71-58aa-a780-c01d04341240" :question/id #uuid "73c135de-ad71-58aa-a780-c01d04341240" :question/math-academy-id "q-221379" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $12∣h$ then $4∣h$\n- If $4∣h$ then $2∣h$\n- If $3∣h$ then $12∣h$" :question/worked-solution "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$ we have transitivity of divisibility:\n\n$a∣b\\,$ and $\\,b∣c$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $a∣c$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, note that $4∣12.$ Therefore, we have\n$4∣12$ and $12∣h,$ which implies that $4∣h.$\n\n- Statement II is true. First, note that $2∣4.$ Therefore, we have\n$2∣4$ and $4∣h,$ which implies that $2∣h.$\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, let $h=3.$ Then, $3∣3$ but $12∤3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-185758a4-16ad-57b8-bf67-872651eda925"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-185758a4-16ad-57b8-bf67-872651eda925" :answer-field/id #uuid "185758a4-16ad-57b8-bf67-872651eda925" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6b4b7a2b-3e52-5afd-8b75-c581575d9429" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6b4b7a2b-3e52-5afd-8b75-c581575d9429" "answer-86a84e34-cc31-5936-aa5b-9bcfb65473f1" "answer-2e1582c6-f975-57a2-bb84-29de70274193" "answer-a39f6118-e6af-5c4f-b439-8c10db5598d8" "answer-5d34d488-7731-54e1-adee-10ba7466acca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b4b7a2b-3e52-5afd-8b75-c581575d9429" :answer/id #uuid "6b4b7a2b-3e52-5afd-8b75-c581575d9429" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86a84e34-cc31-5936-aa5b-9bcfb65473f1" :answer/id #uuid "86a84e34-cc31-5936-aa5b-9bcfb65473f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e1582c6-f975-57a2-bb84-29de70274193" :answer/id #uuid "2e1582c6-f975-57a2-bb84-29de70274193" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a39f6118-e6af-5c4f-b439-8c10db5598d8" :answer/id #uuid "a39f6118-e6af-5c4f-b439-8c10db5598d8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d34d488-7731-54e1-adee-10ba7466acca" :answer/id #uuid "5d34d488-7731-54e1-adee-10ba7466acca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186199012 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $15\\,|\\,32b$ then $15\\,|\\,b$\n- If ${7}^{2}\\,|\\,7b$ then ${7}^{2}\\,|\\,b$\n- If ${3}^{2}\\,|\\,25b$ then $9\\,|\\,b$" :question/worked-solution "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$c\\,|\\,ab\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,c)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $\\,c\\,|\\,b.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(15,32)=1.$ Therefore, we have $15\\,|\\,32b$ and $\\text{gcd}(15,32)=1,$ which implies $15\\,|\\,b.$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, let $b=7.$ Then, ${7}^{2}∣7\\cdot 7$ but ${7}^{2}∤7.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}({3}^{2},25)=1.$ Therefore, we have ${3}^{2}∣25b$ and $\\text{gcd}({3}^{2},25)=1,$ which implies ${3}^{2}\\,|\\,b.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186197942 :answer-field/correct 17592186197945 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-42a248b1-4b2a-5a7f-b673-589ac28da9a8" :question/id #uuid "42a248b1-4b2a-5a7f-b673-589ac28da9a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-93649" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $10\\,|\\,21b$ then $10\\,|\\,b$\n- If $21\\,|\\,25b$ then $21\\,|\\,b$\n- If $15\\,|\\,9b$ then $15\\,|\\,b$" :question/worked-solution "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$c\\,|\\,ab\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,c)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $\\,c\\,|\\,b.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(10,21)=1.$ Therefore, we have $10\\,|\\,21b$ and $\\text{gcd}(10,21)=1,$ which implies $10\\,|\\,b.$\n\n- Statement II is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(21,25)=1.$ Therefore, we have $21\\,|\\,25b$ and $\\text{gcd}(21,25)=1,$ which implies $21\\,|\\,b.$\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, let $b=5.$ Then, $15∣9\\cdot 5$ but $15∤5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dfb4bbf3-86cf-55ec-89a8-e2c06957f446"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dfb4bbf3-86cf-55ec-89a8-e2c06957f446" :answer-field/id #uuid "dfb4bbf3-86cf-55ec-89a8-e2c06957f446" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-df951e81-7965-5468-a3e1-c106088a53a9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-df951e81-7965-5468-a3e1-c106088a53a9" "answer-3cabb55e-40d7-5b81-a1ac-1144923f9b49" "answer-550ce662-95ae-5c42-94f7-d6898e204e74" "answer-25938baa-529b-5f86-828c-2801671fe4d3" "answer-7760ef9f-a800-540a-87c6-3414de29afe6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df951e81-7965-5468-a3e1-c106088a53a9" :answer/id #uuid "df951e81-7965-5468-a3e1-c106088a53a9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3cabb55e-40d7-5b81-a1ac-1144923f9b49" :answer/id #uuid "3cabb55e-40d7-5b81-a1ac-1144923f9b49" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-550ce662-95ae-5c42-94f7-d6898e204e74" :answer/id #uuid "550ce662-95ae-5c42-94f7-d6898e204e74" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25938baa-529b-5f86-828c-2801671fe4d3" :answer/id #uuid "25938baa-529b-5f86-828c-2801671fe4d3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7760ef9f-a800-540a-87c6-3414de29afe6" :answer/id #uuid "7760ef9f-a800-540a-87c6-3414de29afe6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-553ed68f-8e74-5dda-a8b3-cdd3e89c31cb" :question/id #uuid "553ed68f-8e74-5dda-a8b3-cdd3e89c31cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-93650" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If ${19}^{2}\\,|\\,19b$ then ${19}^{2}\\,|\\,b$\n- If $12\\,|\\,35b$ then $12\\,|\\,b$\n- If $22\\,|\\,{7}^{2}b$ then $22\\,|\\,b$" :question/worked-solution "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$c\\,|\\,ab\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,c)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $\\,c\\,|\\,b.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. As a counterexample, let $b=19.$ Then, ${19}^{2}∣19\\cdot 19$ but ${19}^{2}∤19.$\n\n- Statement II is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(12,35)=1.$ Therefore, we have $12\\,|\\,35b$ and $\\text{gcd}(12,35)=1,$ which implies $12\\,|\\,b.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(22,{7}^{2})=1.$ Therefore, we have $22\\,|\\,{7}^{2}b$ and $\\text{gcd}(22,{7}^{2})=1,$ which implies $22\\,|\\,b.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-25f31e32-b105-56ba-945b-18f1eba552b5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-25f31e32-b105-56ba-945b-18f1eba552b5" :answer-field/id #uuid "25f31e32-b105-56ba-945b-18f1eba552b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-06c38ff4-4134-5851-a52f-d46fca4ccc12" :answer-field/choices ["answer-142f0a78-ef1b-5c40-b87c-2e4e6e998e29" "answer-28a1ea30-a1c0-5800-8caf-4ea2604323dc" "answer-afdca230-1900-5d05-8b30-94bc667faa97" "answer-06c38ff4-4134-5851-a52f-d46fca4ccc12" "answer-5bd1e956-1cac-5094-a64b-65c5d077b526"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-142f0a78-ef1b-5c40-b87c-2e4e6e998e29" :answer/id #uuid "142f0a78-ef1b-5c40-b87c-2e4e6e998e29" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28a1ea30-a1c0-5800-8caf-4ea2604323dc" :answer/id #uuid "28a1ea30-a1c0-5800-8caf-4ea2604323dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afdca230-1900-5d05-8b30-94bc667faa97" :answer/id #uuid "afdca230-1900-5d05-8b30-94bc667faa97" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06c38ff4-4134-5851-a52f-d46fca4ccc12" :answer/id #uuid "06c38ff4-4134-5851-a52f-d46fca4ccc12" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5bd1e956-1cac-5094-a64b-65c5d077b526" :answer/id #uuid "5bd1e956-1cac-5094-a64b-65c5d077b526" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f3b9fb7f-2262-5e34-bb97-3a915acfa755" :question/id #uuid "f3b9fb7f-2262-5e34-bb97-3a915acfa755" :question/math-academy-id "q-93648" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If ${3}^{2}\\,|\\,10b$ then ${3}^{2}\\,|\\,b$\n- If ${17}^{2}\\,|\\,17b$ then ${17}^{2}\\,|\\,b$\n- If $20\\,|\\,{3}^{3}b$ then $20\\,|\\,b$" :question/worked-solution "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$c\\,|\\,ab\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,c)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $\\,c\\,|\\,b.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}({3}^{2},10)=1.$ Therefore, we have ${3}^{2}\\,|\\,10b$ and $\\text{gcd}({3}^{2},10)=1,$ which implies ${3}^{2}\\,|\\,b.$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, let $b=17.$ Then, ${17}^{2}∣17\\cdot 17$ but ${17}^{2}∤17.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(20,{3}^{3})=1.$ Therefore, we have $20\\,|\\,{3}^{3}b$ and $\\text{gcd}(20,{3}^{3})=1,$ which implies $20\\,|\\,b.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b5e3230f-cb4f-51e8-a721-e24f62b0c3ea"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b5e3230f-cb4f-51e8-a721-e24f62b0c3ea" :answer-field/id #uuid "b5e3230f-cb4f-51e8-a721-e24f62b0c3ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dcb9bd8f-1205-50c0-a72f-14df58d7f13a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-47123b5a-4d9e-5980-b7e8-1b9b31e1fa9c" "answer-dcb9bd8f-1205-50c0-a72f-14df58d7f13a" "answer-e26579ec-ded1-5c35-9155-e69045a20a37" "answer-a964c9b7-bccb-5c9b-b3c7-48de44c00f07" "answer-8d1afd65-b437-5472-b418-2dc1d6ebe865"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47123b5a-4d9e-5980-b7e8-1b9b31e1fa9c" :answer/id #uuid "47123b5a-4d9e-5980-b7e8-1b9b31e1fa9c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dcb9bd8f-1205-50c0-a72f-14df58d7f13a" :answer/id #uuid "dcb9bd8f-1205-50c0-a72f-14df58d7f13a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e26579ec-ded1-5c35-9155-e69045a20a37" :answer/id #uuid "e26579ec-ded1-5c35-9155-e69045a20a37" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a964c9b7-bccb-5c9b-b3c7-48de44c00f07" :answer/id #uuid "a964c9b7-bccb-5c9b-b3c7-48de44c00f07" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I,II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d1afd65-b437-5472-b418-2dc1d6ebe865" :answer/id #uuid "8d1afd65-b437-5472-b418-2dc1d6ebe865" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5ddd359d-678b-53c8-9991-000fcf922944" :question/id #uuid "5ddd359d-678b-53c8-9991-000fcf922944" :question/math-academy-id "q-93657" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $3\\,|\\,a$ and $2\\,|\\,a$ then $6\\,|\\,a$\n- If $7\\,|\\,b$ and $14\\,|\\,b$ then $98\\,|\\,b$\n- If ${2}^{3}\\,|\\,c$ and $3\\,|\\,c$ then $24\\,|\\,c$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$a\\,|\\,c,$ $\\,b\\,|\\,c,\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,b)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $ab\\,|\\,c$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(2,3)=1$ and $2\\cdot 3=6.$ Therefore, we have $(2\\,|\\,a),(3\\,|\\,a),$ and $\\text{gcd}(2,3)=1,$ which implies $(6\\,|\\,a).$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, let $b=14.$ Then, $(7∣14)$ and $(14∣14),$ but $(98∤14).$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}({2}^{3},3)=1$ and ${2}^{3}\\cdot 3=24.$ Therefore, we have $({2}^{3}\\,|\\,c),(3\\,|\\,c),$ and $\\text{gcd}({2}^{3},3)=1,$ which implies $(24\\,|\\,c).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f237d89a-f9be-5d52-a1df-add8fdc50be1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f237d89a-f9be-5d52-a1df-add8fdc50be1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f237d89a-f9be-5d52-a1df-add8fdc50be1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-da7300a2-932d-5ccd-b80e-d390c021dccf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6b662c83-9382-549d-b78f-d6ae45b36298" "answer-da7300a2-932d-5ccd-b80e-d390c021dccf" "answer-afc58b19-6e0c-5559-867b-c0befae68830" "answer-144822ca-c64b-5d44-988e-8d3f58310385" "answer-ae35d862-ca5e-5f85-a3fd-da77890fb2a6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b662c83-9382-549d-b78f-d6ae45b36298" :answer/id #uuid "6b662c83-9382-549d-b78f-d6ae45b36298" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da7300a2-932d-5ccd-b80e-d390c021dccf" :answer/id #uuid "da7300a2-932d-5ccd-b80e-d390c021dccf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afc58b19-6e0c-5559-867b-c0befae68830" :answer/id #uuid "afc58b19-6e0c-5559-867b-c0befae68830" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-144822ca-c64b-5d44-988e-8d3f58310385" :answer/id #uuid "144822ca-c64b-5d44-988e-8d3f58310385" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae35d862-ca5e-5f85-a3fd-da77890fb2a6" :answer/id #uuid "ae35d862-ca5e-5f85-a3fd-da77890fb2a6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6d7153a0-178f-57d1-b332-d3ea8e076028" :question/id #uuid "6d7153a0-178f-57d1-b332-d3ea8e076028" :question/math-academy-id "q-93658" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $4\\,|\\,a$ and $9\\,|\\,a$ then $36\\,|\\,a$\n- If $5\\,|\\,b$ and $7\\,|\\,b$ then $35\\,|\\,b$\n- If ${6}^{2}\\,|\\,c$ and $2\\,|\\,c$ then $72\\,|\\,c$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$a\\,|\\,c,$ $\\,b\\,|\\,c,\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,b)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $ab\\,|\\,c$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(4,9)=1$ and $4\\cdot 9=36.$ Therefore, we have $(4\\,|\\,a),(9\\,|\\,a),$ and $\\text{gcd}(4,9)=1,$ which implies $(36\\,|\\,a).$\n\n- Statement II is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(5,7)=1$ and $5\\cdot 7=35.$ Therefore, we have $(5\\,|\\,b),(7\\,|\\,b),$ and $\\text{gcd}(5,7)=1,$ which implies $(35\\,|\\,b).$\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, let $c=36.$ Then, $({6}^{2}∣36)$ and $(2∣36),$ but $(72∤36).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9800a386-864d-5b89-9fa0-d8050a82fd2d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9800a386-864d-5b89-9fa0-d8050a82fd2d" :answer-field/id #uuid "9800a386-864d-5b89-9fa0-d8050a82fd2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0cbae4e4-2423-5869-9afa-da82e1b33b03" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0cbae4e4-2423-5869-9afa-da82e1b33b03" "answer-ec1d996a-1c8d-5142-913e-181d70bfe766" "answer-9f28d17f-a614-54b1-8f45-4295cb2a9f09" "answer-c915309d-8abd-5446-a1f9-f241c7dc3116" "answer-63d2cb0f-4fa8-5c73-8c7f-8dfd3f5884fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0cbae4e4-2423-5869-9afa-da82e1b33b03" :answer/id #uuid "0cbae4e4-2423-5869-9afa-da82e1b33b03" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec1d996a-1c8d-5142-913e-181d70bfe766" :answer/id #uuid "ec1d996a-1c8d-5142-913e-181d70bfe766" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f28d17f-a614-54